                <pb facs="1100" n="996" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg996"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90f2/28</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain (Mellon) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 505</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-23">November 23,
                        1932</date>.<lb/>[Received December 7.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s cabled instruction No. 285, November 18, 5 p.m., and to report that
                    in reply to the note which as authorized thereby was on November 19 addressed to
                    the Minister of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia I have now received a communication
                    under date of November 21, a copy of which is enclosed together with the
                    original Arabic text accompanying it.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of Embassy</hi>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d754-a1.xml" xpointer="d754-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
